#: src/app/about/page.tsx:38
#~ msgid "We built a monolithic backend in Rust with PostgreSQL and SeaORM 2.0. We use schemas, PostgreSQL Roles, RLS, Column-Level Privileges, and a type‑safe <0>schema</0> ENUM for hard bounded context isolation. Our unified outbox is driven by <1>LISTEN/NOTIFY</1> for instant event delivery. We use <2>JSONB</2> with graceful degradation for custom field filtering. We enforce strict tenant isolation via private <3>TenantId</3> newtype, database-level roles, RLS, and Column-Level Privileges. PII is redacted at compile time via redacting newtypes with zero runtime overhead; JSON serialization is strictly restricted to the API layer via wrapper structs."
